#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:9
msgid "Doyle-Fuller-Newman Model (DFN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:21
msgid "Model Equations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:32
msgid ""
"The DFN comprises equations for charge and mass conservation in the solid "
"the solid and electrolyte, and also prescribes behaviour for the "
"electrochemical reactions occurring on the interface between the solid an "
"electrolyte. For more information please see `[2] <#References>`__ or other "
"standard texts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:34
msgid ""
"Below we summarise the model, with all parameters give in the table at the "
"end of this notebook. Here we use a roman subscript :math:`\\text{k} \\in "
"\\text{n, s, p}` is used to denote the regions negative electrode, "
"separator, and positive electrode, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:36
msgid "The model equations for the DFN read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:39
msgid "Charge conservation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:41
msgid ""
"\\frac{\\partial i_{\\text{e,k}}}{\\partial x} = \\begin{cases}\n"
"                                                  a_{\\text{k}}"
"j_{\\text{k}}, \\quad &\\text{k} = \\text{n, p}\\\\\n"
"                                                  0, \\qquad &\\text{k} = "
"\\text{s}\n"
"                                            \\end{cases},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:49
msgid ""
"i_{\\text{e,k}} = \\epsilon_{\\text{k}}^{\\text{b}} \\kappa_{\\text{e}}"
"(c_{\\text{e,k}}) \\left( - \\frac{\\partial \\phi_{\\text{e,k}}}{\\partial "
"x} + 2(1-t^+)\\frac{RT}{F}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial "
"x}\\left(\\log(c_{\\text{e,k}})\\right)\\right), \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, s, "
"p}, \\\\\n"
"I-i_{\\text{e,k}} = - \\sigma_{\\text{k}} \\frac{\\partial \\phi_{\\text{e,"
"k}}}{\\partial x}, \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, s, p}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:56
msgid "Mass conservation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:58
msgid ""
"\\epsilon_{\\text{k}} \\frac{\\partial c_{\\text{e,k}}}{\\partial t} = -"
"\\frac{\\partial N_{\\text{e,k}}}{\\partial x} + \\frac{1}"
"{F}\\frac{\\partial i_{\\text{e,k}}}{\\partial x}, \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, "
"s, p},\\\\\n"
"N_{\\text{e,k}} = -\\epsilon_{\\text{k}}^{\\text{b}} D_{\\text{e}}"
"(c_{\\text{e,k}}) \\frac{\\partial c_{\\text{e,k}}}{\\partial x} +  "
"\\frac{t^+}{F} i_{\\text{e,k}},\n"
"\\\\ \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, s, p}, \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\partial c_{\\text{s,k}}}{\\partial t} = -\\frac{1}{r_{\\text{k}}^2} "
"\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial r_{\\text{k}}} \\left(r_{\\text{k}}^2 "
"N_{\\text{s,k}}\\right), \\\\ \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, p},\\\\\n"
"N_{\\text{s,k}} = -D_{\\text{s,k}}(c_{\\text{s,k}}) \\frac{\\partial "
"c_{\\text{s,k}}}{\\partial r_{\\text{k}}}, \\\\ \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, p}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:68
msgid "Electrochemical reactions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:70
msgid ""
"j_{\\text{k}} = 2 j_{\\text{0,k}} \\sinh\\left(\\frac{ F\\eta_{\\text{k}}}"
"{2RT} \\right), \\\\ \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, p}, \\\\\n"
"j_{\\text{0,k}} = c_{\\text{s,k}}^{1/2} (1-c_{\\text{s,k}})^{1/2}c_{\\text{e,"
"k}}^{1/2}\\big|_{r_{\\text{k}}=1}, \\\\ \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, p}, \\\\\n"
"\\eta_{\\text{k}} = \\phi_{\\text{s,k}} - \\phi_{\\text{e,k}} - U_{\\text{k}}"
"(c_{\\text{s,k}}\\big|_{r_{\\text{k}}=1}), \\\\ \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, p}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:77
msgid "These are to be solved subject to the following boundary conditions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:80
msgid "Current:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:82
msgid ""
"i_{\\text{e,n}}\\big|_{x=0} = 0, \\quad i_{\\text{e,p}}\\big|_{x=L}=0,  \\"
"\\\n"
"\\phi_{\\text{e,n}}\\big|_{x=L_{\\text{n}}} = \\phi_{\\text{e,s}}\\big|"
"_{x=L_{\\text{n}}}, \\quad i_{\\text{e,n}}\\big|_{x=L_{\\text{n}}} = "
"i_{\\text{e,s}}\\big\\vert_{x=L_{\\text{n}}} = I, \\\\\n"
"\\phi_{\\text{e,s}}\\big|_{x=L-L_{\\text{p}}} = \\phi_{\\text{e,p}}\\big|"
"_{x=L-L_{\\text{p}}}, \\quad\n"
"    i_{\\text{e,s}}\\big|_{x=L-L_{\\text{p}}} = i_{\\text{e,p}}\\big|_{x=L-"
"L_{\\text{p}}} = I."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:91
msgid "Concentration in the electrolyte:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:93
msgid ""
"N_{\\text{e,n}}\\big|_{x=0} = 0, \\quad N_{\\text{e,p}}\\big|_{x=L}=0,\\\\\n"
"c_{\\text{e,n}}\\big|_{x=L_{\\text{n}}} = c_{\\text{e,s}}|"
"_{x=L_{\\text{n}}}, \\quad N_{\\text{e,n}}\\big|_{x=L_{\\text{n}}}"
"=N_{\\text{e,s}}\\big|_{x=L_{\\text{n}}}, \\\\\n"
"c_{\\text{e,s}}|_{x=L-L_{\\text{p}}}=c_{\\text{e,p}}|_{x=L-L_{\\text{p}}}, "
"\\quad N_{\\text{e,s}}\\big|_{x=L-L_{\\text{p}}}=N_{\\text{e,p}}\\big|_{x=L-"
"L_{\\text{p}}}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:101
msgid "Concentration in the electrode active material:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:103
msgid ""
"N_{\\text{s,k}}\\big|_{r_{\\text{k}}=0} = 0, \\quad \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, "
"p}, \\quad \\ \\ N_{\\text{s,k}}\\big|_{r_{\\text{k}}=R_{\\text{k}}} = "
"\\frac{j_{\\text{k}}}{F}, \\quad \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, p}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:109
msgid "Reference potential:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:111
msgid ""
"\\phi_{\\text{s,cn}} = 0, \\quad  \\boldsymbol{x} \\in \\partial "
"\\Omega_{\\text{tab,n}}.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:114
msgid "And the initial conditions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:116
msgid ""
"c_{\\text{s,k}}(x,r,0) = c_{\\text{s,k,0}}, \\quad \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, "
"p},\\\\\n"
"c_{\\text{e,k}}(x,0) = c_{\\text{e,0}}, \\quad \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, s, "
"p}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:132
msgid "Example solving DFN using PyBaMM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:143
msgid ""
"Below we show how to solve the DFN model, using the default geometry, mesh, "
"parameters, discretisation and solver provided with PyBaMM. For a more "
"detailed example, see the notebook on the `SPM <https://github.com/pybamm-"
"team/PyBaMM/blob/main/docs/source/examples/notebooks/models/SPM.ipynb>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:145
msgid ""
"In order to show off all the different points at which the process of "
"setting up and solving a model in PyBaMM can be customised we explicitly "
"handle the stages of choosing a geometry, setting parameters, discretising "
"the model and solving the model. However, it is often simpler in practice to "
"use the ``Simulation`` class, which handles many of the stages "
"automatically, as shown `here <../simulations_and_experiments/simulation-"
"class.ipynb>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:147
msgid ""
"First we need to import pybamm, along with numpy which we will use in this "
"notebook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:-1
msgid "[1]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"%pip install \"pybamm[plot,cite]\" -q    # install PyBaMM if it is not "
"installed\n"
"import numpy as np\n"
"\n"
"import pybamm"
msgstr ""

