#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:201
msgid ""
"We then load the DFN model and default geometry, and process them both using "
"the default parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:-1
msgid "[2]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"# load model\n"
"model = pybamm.lithium_ion.DFN()\n"
"\n"
"# create geometry\n"
"geometry = model.default_geometry\n"
"\n"
"# load parameter values and process model and geometry\n"
"param = model.default_parameter_values\n"
"param.process_model(model)\n"
"param.process_geometry(geometry)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:231
msgid ""
"The next step is to set the mesh and discretise the model. Again, we choose "
"the default settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:-1
msgid "[3]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"# set mesh\n"
"mesh = pybamm.Mesh(geometry, model.default_submesh_types, model."
"default_var_pts)\n"
"\n"
"# discretise model\n"
"disc = pybamm.Discretisation(mesh, model.default_spatial_methods)\n"
"disc.process_model(model);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:257
msgid ""
"The model is now ready to be solved. We select the default DAE solver for "
"the DFN. Note that in order to successfully solve the system of DAEs we are "
"required to give consistent initial conditions. This is handled "
"automatically by PyBaMM during the solve operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:-1
msgid "[4]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"# solve model\n"
"solver = model.default_solver\n"
"t_eval = np.linspace(0, 3600, 300)  # time in seconds\n"
"solution = solver.solve(model, t_eval)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:281
msgid ""
"To get a quick overview of the model outputs we can use the QuickPlot class, "
"which plots a common set of useful outputs. The method ``Quickplot."
"dynamic_plot`` makes a slider widget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:-1
msgid "[8]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/DFN.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"quick_plot = pybamm.QuickPlot(\n"
"    solution, [\"Positive electrode interfacial current density [A.m-2]\"]\n"
")\n"
"quick_plot.dynamic_plot();"
msgstr ""

